# Architecture

Project type: `{{ project_type }}`. Runtime level: `{{ runtime_level }}`.
Governance: `{{ governance }}`.

This document describes the architecture generated now. Future extensions are
listed separately so they do not read as already implemented.

## Current Architecture

{% if project_type == "script" %}
The generated system is a Python CLI package.

```text
tests -> src/{{ python_package }}/__main__.py -> package code
```

`make run` executes the package module. `make test`, `make lint`,
`make typecheck`, and `make build` verify the local package lifecycle. There is
no service runtime, browser runtime, generated client, container runtime, or
external infrastructure in this profile.
{% elif project_type == "library" %}
The generated system is a Python library package.

```text
consumer code -> src/{{ python_package }}/__init__.py -> package internals
```

The package exports its public API from `__init__.py` and includes `py.typed` for
typed consumers. `make build` writes distribution artifacts to `dist/`. There is
no CLI entry point, service runtime, browser runtime, generated client, or
external infrastructure in this profile.
{% elif project_type == "backend" %}
The generated system is a FastAPI service.

```text
HTTP routes -> application use cases -> domain model
```

The app entry point is `backend/src/app/main.py`. Feature code is organized
under `backend/src/app/modules/`, and shared configuration/observability code is
under `backend/src/app/shared/`. The generated service exposes `/health`,
`/ready`, and `/openapi.json`. There is no frontend runtime or generated
frontend client in this profile.
{% elif project_type == "frontend" %}
The generated system is a Nuxt application.

```text
pages -> feature components -> feature composables
```

The application lives in `frontend/`. Pages compose feature components, feature
logic belongs under `frontend/features/`, and build output is written to
`frontend/.output/`. There is no backend runtime or generated client in this
profile.
{% elif project_type == "fullstack" %}
The generated system is a FastAPI backend and Nuxt frontend.

```text
Nuxt page -> generated TypeScript client -> FastAPI route -> application use case -> domain model
```

The backend app entry point is `backend/src/app/main.py`. Backend feature code is
organized under `backend/src/app/modules/`, with shared configuration and
observability under `backend/src/app/shared/`. The frontend lives in
`frontend/`, with pages, feature components, and shared API runtime code.

`make api-schema` exports the backend OpenAPI contract. `make api-generate`
writes the generated TypeScript client. `make api-check` fails when that client
drifts from the backend schema.
{% if runtime_level == "production" %}

The production runtime currently consists of two local OCI image artifacts:

- backend image running Uvicorn from an installed Python environment
- frontend image running the Nuxt server output with Node

Compose is used only as local artifact verification. It wires ports, health
checks, service ordering, and shutdown for `make prod-up`, `make prod-status`,
`make prod-smoke`, and `make prod-down`.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

